# Allowlist, not a blocklist: ignore everything, then re-admit exactly what
# `cargo build -p sunrise-server` needs.
#
# The inverted form is deliberate. A blocklist has to be amended every time the
# repository grows a directory, and the failure mode is silent: this tree
# currently carries a 6 GB `target/` and a 284 MB `node_modules/`, either of
# which lands in the build context the day someone forgets an entry —
# invalidating the cache on every build and shipping bytes nobody inspected.
# Here a new directory is excluded until someone says otherwise.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml

# Both forms per directory. `!crates` re-admits the directory so the walk
# descends into it at all; `!crates/**` re-admits what is inside. Relying on
# either alone is relying on an implementation detail of how a given builder
# prunes excluded subtrees.
!crates
!crates/**

# Re-exclusions inside the admitted tree. A per-crate `target/` appears
# whenever someone runs cargo from inside one crate; the workspace `target/` is
# already covered by the leading `*`.
crates/**/target
crates/**/*.rs.bk
**/.DS_Store
